WEBVTT

NOTE Sentence windows use measured synthesized WAV sample counts.
Picture boundaries round to nearest frame, ties upward.
Captions are also burned into the MP4.

N1
00:00:01.208 --> 00:00:10.292
This project studies how managerial speech relates to firm behavior, with CEO risk preference as the first measurement setting.

N2
00:00:10.333 --> 00:00:15.708
Speech may express a manager's perspective, but it also serves an audience.

N3
00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:21.542
Research and development spending reflects choices, opportunities, and constraints.

N4
00:00:21.583 --> 00:00:26.083
A model can learn an association between these two sources.

N5
00:00:26.125 --> 00:00:31.125
Whether its prediction measures risk preference requires separate evidence.

N6
00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:41.625
This walkthrough explains the four existing stages, their assembled agent connections, and what the offline demonstration actually establishes.

N7
00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:46.583
The scientific packages and their received results already exist.

N8
00:00:46.625 --> 00:00:51.833
The new work connects them through stage adapters and a resumable workflow.

N9
00:00:51.875 --> 00:01:01.792
During this assembly, no fresh scientific screening, empirical model training, finance reconstruction, or Stata estimation was executed.

N10
00:01:01.833 --> 00:01:06.667
The earlier eight-topic agent demonstration remains available.

N11
00:01:06.708 --> 00:01:12.958
The connected demonstration uses three invented topics and scripted model replies.

N12
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:22.917
These distinctions matter: received results, implemented interfaces, and newly executed empirical evidence are different claims.

N13
00:01:22.958 --> 00:01:29.458
Step one connects the saved topic catalogue and the delivered matrix of topic densities.

N14
00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:33.833
The study fixes three hundred and fifty-four topic columns.

N15
00:01:33.875 --> 00:01:40.917
The adapter checks the catalogue, matrix dimensions, and model identity when inference is requested.

N16
00:01:40.958 --> 00:01:45.708
Optional inference reuses the existing topic-model code.

N17
00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:51.083
For the saved matrix, historical row ordering is taken from the delivery.

N18
00:01:51.125 --> 00:01:56.500
This assembly does not independently authenticate that original ordering.

N19
00:01:56.542 --> 00:02:00.208
It also retains the supplied sentiment input.

N20
00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:04.875
It does not create sentiment measurements for a new corpus.

N21
00:02:04.917 --> 00:02:08.750
Fresh screening begins with three independent readers.

N22
00:02:08.792 --> 00:02:15.292
Each reader labels the complete descriptor catalogue for binary relevance to risk preference.

N23
00:02:15.333 --> 00:02:19.042
The readers do not divide the topics between them.

N24
00:02:19.083 --> 00:02:24.542
Each makes an initial judgment about all three hundred and fifty-four topics.

N25
00:02:24.583 --> 00:02:30.958
All three initial responses must be sealed before any reader receives source passages.

N26
00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:34.667
This is the barrier between the two reading stages.

N27
00:02:34.708 --> 00:02:40.667
The fresh-reader default is GPT six Astra at extra-high reasoning effort.

N28
00:02:40.708 --> 00:02:46.292
These defaults were not validated with live calls during assembly.

N29
00:02:46.333 --> 00:02:56.042
In stage B, each reader continues its own history through eighteen review pages containing one thousand and sixty-two source passages.

N30
00:02:56.083 --> 00:03:02.208
Each sees its own initial labels and the source material, without the other readers' votes.

N31
00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:05.792
Initial judgments remain separately available.

N32
00:03:05.833 --> 00:03:13.458
The original toolkit exports a two-of-three majority for relevance, alongside reasons and minority votes.

N33
00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:16.333
Confidence does not weight the votes.

N34
00:03:16.375 --> 00:03:25.250
The delivered primary selection contains three hundred and twenty-one topics from Astra, extra-high effort, repetition one.

N35
00:03:25.292 --> 00:03:30.417
Its use does not establish superiority over other trials.

N36
00:03:30.458 --> 00:03:37.708
Step three passes the selected topic identifiers to the supplied input builder and training script.

N37
00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:42.583
The predictors are selected topic features and aggregate sentiment.

N38
00:03:42.625 --> 00:03:48.292
The outcome is research and development spending divided by total assets.

N39
00:03:48.333 --> 00:03:54.708
The original Ridge and XGBoost implementations retain their seeds and tuning grids.

N40
00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:59.083
Firm and CEO connected groups define five folds.

N41
00:03:59.125 --> 00:04:04.625
Each out-of-fold score comes from a model trained outside its held-out group.

N42
00:04:04.667 --> 00:04:08.417
Firms that share a CEO remain in the same group.

N43
00:04:08.458 --> 00:04:12.333
The saved topic representation remains fixed.

N44
00:04:12.375 --> 00:04:18.167
These are contemporaneous predictions, rather than forecasts of future behavior.

N45
00:04:18.208 --> 00:04:26.083
The implemented method does not first collapse topics into the earlier blueprint’s scalar narrative measure.

N46
00:04:26.125 --> 00:04:34.375
The supplied target replaces missing research and development spending with zero, provided that total assets are positive.

N47
00:04:34.417 --> 00:04:39.875
Rows with missing or nonpositive assets do not enter model training.

N48
00:04:39.917 --> 00:04:42.958
They still receive held-out predictions.

N49
00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:48.458
Selected topic densities use a centered log-ratio transformation.

N50
00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:52.792
Topic features and aggregate sentiment are standardized.

N51
00:04:52.833 --> 00:04:57.125
Imputation and scaling are fitted within training data.

N52
00:04:57.167 --> 00:05:03.917
Target winsorization also uses training data, and tuning stays inside the training folds.

N53
00:05:03.958 --> 00:05:07.417
Missing spending can mean missing disclosure.

N54
00:05:07.458 --> 00:05:15.458
Consequently, the prediction can reflect reporting and industry patterns as well as managerial behavior.

N55
00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:21.708
Step four receives the newly generated score file through the original local matcher.

N56
00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:26.250
The original rich identity panel remains the matching source.

N57
00:05:26.292 --> 00:05:30.417
The adapter checks panel keys and fold identities.

N58
00:05:30.458 --> 00:05:36.792
Negative out-of-fold predictions are clipped to zero, then multiplied by one hundred.

N59
00:05:36.833 --> 00:05:43.333
This score is in percentage points of predicted research and development relative to assets.

N60
00:05:43.375 --> 00:05:45.958
It is not a percentile rank.

N61
00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:50.708
Model preparation retains the same twenty-five formulas.

N62
00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:54.750
It is a separate stage from estimation in Stata.

N63
00:05:54.792 --> 00:06:01.375
A completed preparation stage means that model inputs and the estimation script are ready.

N64
00:06:01.417 --> 00:06:05.375
It does not mean regressions have been run.

N65
00:06:05.417 --> 00:06:09.792
The downstream outcome is whether the firm pays dividends.

N66
00:06:09.833 --> 00:06:13.875
The supplied specifications use logit models.

N67
00:06:13.917 --> 00:06:22.292
Nine replication specifications accompany sixteen score specifications, for twenty-five formulas in total.

N68
00:06:22.333 --> 00:06:32.625
The score specifications enter Ridge and XGBoost separately, alongside financial and compensation controls and industry and year effects.

N69
00:06:32.667 --> 00:06:39.917
One set includes actual research and development relative to assets and its missingness indicator.

N70
00:06:39.958 --> 00:06:42.292
The other omits both.

N71
00:06:42.333 --> 00:06:47.958
These comparisons examine conditional association with dividend payment.

N72
00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:53.750
They do not by themselves establish causality or construct validity.

N73
00:06:53.792 --> 00:07:00.458
The coordinator has four named tools: get status, run stage, read result, and finish.

N74
00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:03.917
These connect the model to the shared workflow.

N75
00:07:03.958 --> 00:07:07.042
The dispatcher enforces stage order.

N76
00:07:07.083 --> 00:07:14.083
Both direct execution and agent execution use the same saved state and artifact checks.

N77
00:07:14.125 --> 00:07:19.250
A coordinator's completion claim cannot complete an unfinished stage.

N78
00:07:19.292 --> 00:07:25.708
The saved outputs determine completion, and completed artifacts are checked again on resume.

N79
00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:32.000
The coordinator cannot issue arbitrary commands or redefine the scientific method.

N80
00:07:32.042 --> 00:07:39.167
Constructs, specifications, and the interpretation of evidence remain research decisions.

N81
00:07:39.208 --> 00:07:45.083
The offline example uses two fabricated rows and three invented topics.

N82
00:07:45.125 --> 00:07:49.083
Its selection contains topic one and topic three.

N83
00:07:49.125 --> 00:07:53.708
For the first row, the selected weights sum to zero point seven.

N84
00:07:53.750 --> 00:07:57.125
For the second, they sum to zero point eight.

N85
00:07:57.167 --> 00:08:02.250
Those toy scores are written to a file and carried into the step four input.

N86
00:08:02.292 --> 00:08:08.250
They are wiring arithmetic, with no trained-model or scientific interpretation.

N87
00:08:08.292 --> 00:08:17.083
The saved summary states that this is a demonstration, with no live model calls, no training, and no estimation.

N88
00:08:17.125 --> 00:08:22.583
The connected demonstration was executed and then resumed for this walkthrough.

N89
00:08:22.625 --> 00:08:26.167
Both runs returned demonstration complete.

N90
00:08:26.208 --> 00:08:32.292
State, event history, stage requests, and results provide a record of the connection.

N91
00:08:32.333 --> 00:08:38.292
Resume verifies completed artifacts rather than relying on a narrative assurance.

N92
00:08:38.333 --> 00:08:44.250
Fresh screening also preserves reader requests, first responses, and sealed pages.

N93
00:08:44.292 --> 00:08:49.875
Invalid or unresolved attempts remain visible for explicit recovery.

N94
00:08:49.917 --> 00:08:55.833
The adapter does not silently repair labels or repeat uncertain first requests.

N95
00:08:55.875 --> 00:09:01.917
This is a property of the workflow, not a guarantee of scientific correctness.

N96
00:09:01.958 --> 00:09:08.875
The assembly's recorded checks cover handoffs, reader independence, stage ordering, and recovery.

N97
00:09:08.917 --> 00:09:12.917
They use fixtures and mocked scientific execution.

N98
00:09:12.958 --> 00:09:18.833
The original scientific packages and their results remain distinct from these checks.

N99
00:09:18.875 --> 00:09:25.000
Reproduction requires the complete assets and the specified scientific runtimes.

N100
00:09:25.042 --> 00:09:35.833
Prediction of research and development spending does not by itself establish psychological risk preference, causality, or superiority over other measures.

N101
00:09:35.875 --> 00:09:41.167
The current contribution is a connected and inspectable implementation.

N102
00:09:41.208 --> 00:09:49.917
An empirical run and independent construct validation remain separate research tasks.
